Comparable vs Comparator

In java both comparable and comparator are interface used for sorting and ordering objects, but they serve different pupose and used in different ways

Comparable
1) It is a interface in Java
2) Comparable provide compareTo() method to sort object.
3) Comparable is a part of java.lang. package
4) Comparable can be used for natural or default ordering
5) Comparable provides a single sorting seg. Eg Sort either by name of id.
6) Comparable modifies the class the implement is
7) We can sort the list elements of Comparable type by Collections.sort(List) method


Comparator
1) Comparator is a functional interface in Java.
2) Comparator provides compare() method to sort object.
3) Comparator is a part of java.util package
4) Comparator can be used for custom ordering
5) Comparator provides multiple sorting sequence. Eg sort by both id & name.
6) Compartor doesn't modify the clsss
7) We can sort the list elements of comparator type by Collections.sort(list, comparator) method i.e( Collections.sort(list, classNameOfComparator) )